    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Four correlations go into one CHSH score. Local pre-set-answer models stop at 2. Quantum mechanics reaches 2 root 2. The extra point eight three comes from geometry.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Show exactly where the CHSH score becomes 2 root 2.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — BELL TESTS",
            "segment": "Bell's Number",
            "greeting": "Jambo, Liam",
            "runningText": "placing four measurement axes…",
            "output": [
              "Local hidden-variable bound: |S| <= 2.",
              "Bell-state prediction: |S| = 2 sqrt(2)."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.46,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Alice chooses one of two axes, A one or A two. Bob chooses B one or B two. Every run returns plus one or minus one, and repeated runs estimate four correlations.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.33,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "CHSH combines them as E eleven plus E twelve plus E twenty-one minus E twenty-two. The minus sign is the hinge that makes four settings test one local model.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.71,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "If outcomes are fixed by local hidden variables, the absolute average score cannot exceed 2, assuming the settings are independently chosen. That is the Bell-CHSH bound, not a limit on one correlation.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.48,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "For the Bell state phi plus, measurements in one plane have correlation cosine of the angle difference. Now place Alice at zero and ninety degrees.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.92,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "Place Bob halfway between those directions: B one at forty-five degrees and B two at minus forty-five degrees. Every relevant separation is forty-five degrees except the last, which is one hundred thirty-five.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "drawon"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.78,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Cosine forty-five degrees is one over root two. So the first three correlations are plus one over root two. Cosine one hundred thirty-five is minus one over root two.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.39,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 9,
      "narration_text": "CHSH subtracts that negative fourth term. Four equal positive contributions remain: four over root two.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.4,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Four divided by root two simplifies to 2 root 2 — about 2.828. That is roughly forty-one percent above 2.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.94,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The violation is not perfect correlation by itself; classical models can do that. It is the pattern across four incompatible setting pairs that no single local pre-set-answer assignment reproduces.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.27,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Bell tests have repeatedly observed CHSH violations. The careful conclusion is that local hidden-variable models satisfying the test's independence assumptions cannot explain the data — not that faster-than-light messages become possible.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.76,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The verdict: 2 is the local hidden-variable ceiling. The four-angle cosine pattern reaches 2 root 2. Bell's number is geometry turned into an experimental discriminator.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.62,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T22:38:31"
      }
    },
